§§ `חלק 6 פרק 5: עסקאות עם בעלי ענין`
-- 268: a controlling shareholder is one who has control under the Securities Law, or 25% of the voting rights (with the holdings of others who have a personal interest in the same transaction, if he has one) while no other person holds more than 50%.
-- Arguments: his holding; control under the Securities Law; he has a personal interest in the transaction; the holdings of the others with such an interest, in total; the largest holding of another person.
